Opens Event Viewer in Windows. There you can manually browse system logs, errors, warnings, logins, PowerShell activity, etc.

eventvwr.msc

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Shows the last 50 events from the System log. These include driver errors, restarts, service issues, disk issues, and network problems

Get-WinEvent -LogName System -MaxEvents 50

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Shows the last 50 security events, e.g. user logins, failed logins, and permission changes. Often requires running PowerShell as administrator.

Get-WinEvent -LogName Security -MaxEvents 50

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Shows the last 50 events related to PowerShell. You can check whether any scripts/commands were run in PowerShell

Get-WinEvent -LogName "Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational" -MaxEvents 50

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Shows the last 50 events from Windows Defender, e.g. threat detections, scans, blocks, and protection updates.

Get-WinEvent -ProviderName "Microsoft-Windows-Windows Defender" -MaxEvents 50


